node_modules/
dist/
# The SSR bundle the prerender step builds and imports. Build output like
# `dist`, and never published: it is deliberately kept OUT of `dist`, which is
# collected wholesale and shipped to R2.
dist-ssr/
# produced by `tsr generate` before every build
src/routeTree.gen.ts

# KIT-WIDE SWEEP SCRATCH — a harness that renders or typechecks all 2,112
# components at once leaves these behind, and committing one is expensive in a
# way that is not obvious. `tsconfig.json` includes `src/**/*.ts`, and
# `src/__all_entry.ts` re-exports every component, so TypeScript follows it into
# the whole kit and the `exclude` that keeps a customer build fast is defeated:
# measured 2026-08-12, `tsc -p tsconfig.json` went 3.9s -> 32.4s, 8.4x, on every
# build. `Dockerfile` does `COPY lovable/template/ ./`, so anything committed
# here is in the build image too.
__sweep/
src/__all_entry.ts
# test/integration/kit-render.mjs's entry point and bundle. Removed in a
# `finally`, which a killed process skips — and `Dockerfile` does
# `COPY lovable/template/ ./`, so a leftover would ride into the build image.
.kitrender/
# A contact sheet of the kit's primitives rendered against the REAL stylesheet,
# plus its screenshots and probe scripts — the only way to answer "what does our
# CSS look like", since every other harness here reads structure rather than
# pixels. Same reasoning as `.kitrender/` above: `Dockerfile` does
# `COPY lovable/template/ ./`, and this is ~2MB of PNGs and throwaway `.tsx`.
.kitsheet/
